{
  "version": 2,
  "about": [
    "The shared equality + serialization spec for every codegrind runner.",
    "",
    "Each language's harness hand-writes its own deepEqual and its own canonical",
    "JSON serializer, because the alternative -- shipping one implementation into",
    "three runtimes -- means embedding a JS engine in the Python image or a JSON",
    "library in the JS one. Hand-written comparators DRIFT. This file is what",
    "keeps them honest: one fixture, read by all of them, checked at BUILD time by",
    "`<runner> --selftest`, which bin/build-runner-image runs as a post-build gate.",
    "An image whose comparator disagrees with this file does not get published.",
    "",
    "Verified by JavaScript today. Python and Java must pass this same file",
    "unmodified when they land; a case that cannot hold across runtimes does not",
    "belong here."
  ],
  "encoding": {
    "sentinels": [
      "Values are plain JSON, with one escape hatch: an object of the exact shape",
      "{\"$cg\": \"<name>\"} is a SENTINEL and must be decoded to the named native",
      "value before comparison or serialization. JSON has no way to write NaN, and",
      "NaN is precisely the comparison every hand-written deepEqual gets wrong.",
      "",
      "  {\"$cg\":\"nan\"}   -> the IEEE-754 quiet NaN",
      "  {\"$cg\":\"inf\"}   -> positive infinity",
      "  {\"$cg\":\"-inf\"}  -> negative infinity",
      "  {\"$cg\":\"-zero\"} -> negative zero",
      "",
      "Decoding is recursive: a sentinel may appear anywhere a value may appear.",
      "An object with a $cg key and any other key is NOT a sentinel -- it is an",
      "ordinary object that happens to have an awkward key, and must be treated as",
      "one."
    ],
    "floatTolerance": [
      "LANDED IN v2 (Phase 3). Two numbers are equal when",
      "",
      "  abs(a-b) <= max(1e-9, 1e-9 * max(abs(a), abs(b)))",
      "",
      "an absolute floor of 1e-9 near zero, relative 1e-9 elsewhere. Without it any",
      "problem that averages anything bakes 0.30000000000000004 into `expected` at",
      "canonicalization time and then rejects the correct answer.",
      "",
      "THREE GUARDS, and every one of them is load-bearing:",
      "",
      "1. NaN and the infinities never reach the tolerance. abs(inf - -inf) is inf",
      "   and 1e-9*inf is also inf, and inf <= inf is TRUE -- so an unguarded",
      "   tolerance would quietly make positive and negative infinity equal. Both",
      "   operands must be finite before any tolerance is considered. `infinity is",
      "   signed` below is the case that catches this.",
      "",
      "2. WHEN BOTH VALUES ARE INTEGERS THEY ARE COMPARED EXACTLY, never with a",
      "   tolerance. A relative tolerance of 1e-9 on a value near 2^53 is an",
      "   absolute slack of about 9 million, which would make `large safe integers",
      "   differing by one` compare EQUAL and silently accept a wrong count, index",
      "   or sum. Counts are exact quantities; only fractions have rounding noise.",
      "   `integers are compared exactly, never with tolerance` pins it directly.",
      "",
      "3. It applies only to numbers -- pairwise, at every position in a structure.",
      "   Array length and object key sets are still compared exactly.",
      "",
      "A value that is integral compares as an integer whatever its runtime type:",
      "JavaScript has one number type, and Python's 2 and 2.0 must not disagree",
      "about a rule this consequential. `integer-valued float equals integer` and",
      "`a float a hair away from an integer is within tolerance` are the pair that",
      "fixes that reading: exact when BOTH sides are integral, tolerant as soon as",
      "either side carries a fraction."
    ]
  },
  "equality": [
    { "name": "identical integers", "a": 1, "b": 1, "equal": true },
    { "name": "different integers", "a": 1, "b": 2, "equal": false },
    { "name": "number is not its string", "a": 1, "b": "1", "equal": false },
    { "name": "true is not one", "a": true, "b": 1, "equal": false },
    { "name": "false is not zero", "a": false, "b": 0, "equal": false },
    { "name": "false is not empty string", "a": false, "b": "", "equal": false },
    { "name": "identical booleans", "a": true, "b": true, "equal": true },
    { "name": "identical strings", "a": "abc", "b": "abc", "equal": true },
    { "name": "strings are case sensitive", "a": "abc", "b": "ABC", "equal": false },
    { "name": "empty string equals empty string", "a": "", "b": "", "equal": true },
    { "name": "null equals null", "a": null, "b": null, "equal": true },
    { "name": "null is not zero", "a": null, "b": 0, "equal": false },
    { "name": "null is not empty string", "a": null, "b": "", "equal": false },
    { "name": "null is not an empty array", "a": null, "b": [], "equal": false },
    { "name": "null is not an empty object", "a": null, "b": {}, "equal": false },
    { "name": "float equal to itself", "a": 1.5, "b": 1.5, "equal": true },
    { "name": "integer-valued float equals integer", "a": 2.0, "b": 2, "equal": true },
    { "name": "large safe integer", "a": 9007199254740991, "b": 9007199254740991, "equal": true },
    { "name": "large safe integers differing by one", "a": 9007199254740991, "b": 9007199254740990, "equal": false },
    { "name": "negative numbers", "a": -7, "b": -7, "equal": true },
    { "name": "sign matters", "a": -7, "b": 7, "equal": false },

    { "name": "float rounding noise is within tolerance", "a": 0.30000000000000004, "b": 0.3, "equal": true },
    { "name": "a real float difference is outside tolerance", "a": 0.3, "b": 0.4, "equal": false },
    { "name": "a float a hair away from an integer is within tolerance", "a": 2.0000000001, "b": 2, "equal": true },
    { "name": "a sum of thirds is within tolerance of one", "a": 0.9999999999999999, "b": 1, "equal": true },
    { "name": "tolerance is relative at large magnitudes", "a": 1234567.8901234, "b": 1234567.8901235, "equal": true },
    { "name": "a large-magnitude float difference is still outside tolerance", "a": 1234567.8901234, "b": 1234567.9, "equal": false },
    { "name": "the absolute floor applies near zero", "a": 1e-10, "b": 0, "equal": true },
    { "name": "just above the absolute floor is not equal", "a": 1e-8, "b": 0, "equal": false },
    { "name": "integers are compared exactly, never with tolerance", "a": 1000000000, "b": 1000000001, "equal": false },
    { "name": "tolerance never reaches an infinity", "a": { "$cg": "inf" }, "b": 1e300, "equal": false },
    { "name": "tolerance never rescues NaN against a number", "a": { "$cg": "nan" }, "b": 0.3, "equal": false },
    { "name": "float tolerance applies inside an array", "a": [1, 0.30000000000000004], "b": [1, 0.3], "equal": true },
    { "name": "float tolerance applies inside an object", "a": { "avg": 0.30000000000000004 }, "b": { "avg": 0.3 }, "equal": true },
    { "name": "tolerance does not paper over a wrong array length", "a": [0.30000000000000004], "b": [0.3, 0.3], "equal": false },

    { "name": "NaN equals NaN", "a": { "$cg": "nan" }, "b": { "$cg": "nan" }, "equal": true },
    { "name": "NaN does not equal zero", "a": { "$cg": "nan" }, "b": 0, "equal": false },
    { "name": "NaN does not equal null", "a": { "$cg": "nan" }, "b": null, "equal": false },
    { "name": "NaN nested in an array", "a": [1, { "$cg": "nan" }], "b": [1, { "$cg": "nan" }], "equal": true },
    { "name": "NaN nested in an object", "a": { "x": { "$cg": "nan" } }, "b": { "x": { "$cg": "nan" } }, "equal": true },
    { "name": "infinity equals infinity", "a": { "$cg": "inf" }, "b": { "$cg": "inf" }, "equal": true },
    { "name": "infinity is signed", "a": { "$cg": "inf" }, "b": { "$cg": "-inf" }, "equal": false },
    { "name": "infinity is not NaN", "a": { "$cg": "inf" }, "b": { "$cg": "nan" }, "equal": false },
    { "name": "negative zero equals zero", "a": { "$cg": "-zero" }, "b": 0, "equal": true },

    { "name": "empty arrays", "a": [], "b": [], "equal": true },
    { "name": "identical arrays", "a": [1, 2, 3], "b": [1, 2, 3], "equal": true },
    { "name": "arrays are ORDER SENSITIVE", "a": [1, 2, 3], "b": [3, 2, 1], "equal": false },
    { "name": "array length matters", "a": [1, 2], "b": [1, 2, 3], "equal": false },
    { "name": "a prefix is not the whole", "a": [1, 2, 3], "b": [1, 2], "equal": false },
    { "name": "nested arrays", "a": [[1, 2], [3]], "b": [[1, 2], [3]], "equal": true },
    { "name": "nested arrays differ deep", "a": [[1, 2], [3]], "b": [[1, 2], [4]], "equal": false },
    { "name": "nesting depth matters", "a": [[1]], "b": [1], "equal": false },
    { "name": "array of strings", "a": ["a", "b"], "b": ["a", "b"], "equal": true },
    { "name": "array of mixed types", "a": [1, "1", true, null], "b": [1, "1", true, null], "equal": true },
    { "name": "empty array is not empty object", "a": [], "b": {}, "equal": false },

    { "name": "empty objects", "a": {}, "b": {}, "equal": true },
    { "name": "identical objects", "a": { "a": 1, "b": 2 }, "b": { "a": 1, "b": 2 }, "equal": true },
    { "name": "objects are KEY-ORDER INSENSITIVE", "a": { "a": 1, "b": 2 }, "b": { "b": 2, "a": 1 }, "equal": true },
    { "name": "an extra key breaks equality", "a": { "a": 1 }, "b": { "a": 1, "b": 2 }, "equal": false },
    { "name": "a missing key breaks equality", "a": { "a": 1, "b": 2 }, "b": { "a": 1 }, "equal": false },
    { "name": "same key count, different keys", "a": { "a": 1 }, "b": { "b": 1 }, "equal": false },
    { "name": "same keys, different values", "a": { "a": 1 }, "b": { "a": 2 }, "equal": false },
    { "name": "a null-valued key is still a key", "a": { "a": null }, "b": {}, "equal": false },
    { "name": "nested objects", "a": { "x": { "y": [1, { "z": 2 }] } }, "b": { "x": { "y": [1, { "z": 2 }] } }, "equal": true },
    { "name": "nested objects differ deep", "a": { "x": { "y": [1, { "z": 2 }] } }, "b": { "x": { "y": [1, { "z": 3 }] } }, "equal": false },
    { "name": "object in array, keys reordered", "a": [{ "a": 1, "b": 2 }], "b": [{ "b": 2, "a": 1 }], "equal": true },
    { "name": "numeric-looking string keys", "a": { "1": "a", "2": "b" }, "b": { "2": "b", "1": "a" }, "equal": true },
    { "name": "a $cg key with siblings is an ordinary object", "a": { "$cg": "nan", "k": 1 }, "b": { "k": 1, "$cg": "nan" }, "equal": true },

    { "name": "matrix", "a": [[1, 0], [0, 1]], "b": [[1, 0], [0, 1]], "equal": true },
    { "name": "matrix rows are ordered", "a": [[1, 0], [0, 1]], "b": [[0, 1], [1, 0]], "equal": false },
    { "name": "list of records", "a": [{ "id": 1, "tags": ["x"] }], "b": [{ "tags": ["x"], "id": 1 }], "equal": true },
    { "name": "deeply mixed structure", "a": { "r": [1, [2, { "s": null }], "t"] }, "b": { "r": [1, [2, { "s": null }], "t"] }, "equal": true }
  ],
  "serialization": [
    {
      "name": "object keys are sorted",
      "value": { "b": 1, "a": 2 },
      "json": "{\"a\":2,\"b\":1}"
    },
    {
      "name": "sorting is recursive",
      "value": { "z": { "d": 1, "c": 2 }, "y": 3 },
      "json": "{\"y\":3,\"z\":{\"c\":2,\"d\":1}}"
    },
    {
      "name": "sorting reaches inside arrays",
      "value": [{ "b": 1, "a": 2 }],
      "json": "[{\"a\":2,\"b\":1}]"
    },
    {
      "name": "array order is PRESERVED, never sorted",
      "value": [3, 1, 2],
      "json": "[3,1,2]"
    },
    {
      "name": "no whitespace between tokens",
      "value": { "a": [1, 2], "b": { "c": 3 } },
      "json": "{\"a\":[1,2],\"b\":{\"c\":3}}"
    },
    {
      "name": "keys sort by code unit, so uppercase precedes lowercase",
      "value": { "b": 1, "B": 2, "a": 3, "A": 4 },
      "json": "{\"A\":4,\"B\":2,\"a\":3,\"b\":1}"
    },
    {
      "name": "digit keys sort as strings",
      "value": { "10": 1, "9": 2, "1": 3 },
      "json": "{\"1\":3,\"10\":1,\"9\":2}"
    },
    { "name": "empty object", "value": {}, "json": "{}" },
    { "name": "empty array", "value": [], "json": "[]" },
    { "name": "null", "value": null, "json": "null" },
    { "name": "true", "value": true, "json": "true" },
    { "name": "false", "value": false, "json": "false" },
    { "name": "integer", "value": 42, "json": "42" },
    { "name": "negative integer", "value": -42, "json": "-42" },
    { "name": "zero", "value": 0, "json": "0" },
    { "name": "integer-valued float has no trailing .0", "value": 2.0, "json": "2" },
    { "name": "float", "value": 1.5, "json": "1.5" },
    { "name": "largest safe integer", "value": 9007199254740991, "json": "9007199254740991" },
    { "name": "plain string", "value": "abc", "json": "\"abc\"" },
    { "name": "empty string", "value": "", "json": "\"\"" },
    { "name": "double quote is escaped", "value": "a\"b", "json": "\"a\\\"b\"" },
    { "name": "backslash is escaped", "value": "a\\b", "json": "\"a\\\\b\"" },
    { "name": "newline is escaped short", "value": "a\nb", "json": "\"a\\nb\"" },
    { "name": "tab is escaped short", "value": "a\tb", "json": "\"a\\tb\"" },
    { "name": "non-ascii is emitted literally, not \\u-escaped", "value": "héllo", "json": "\"héllo\"" },
    { "name": "forward slash is NOT escaped", "value": "a/b", "json": "\"a/b\"" },
    { "name": "nested structure", "value": { "b": [1, { "d": 4, "c": 3 }], "a": null }, "json": "{\"a\":null,\"b\":[1,{\"c\":3,\"d\":4}]}" }
  ]
}
